[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4791584733","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4791584733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":4791584733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHZnH3Q","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-24T16:42:09Z","updated_at":"2026-06-24T16:42:09Z","body":"This pull request reminds me of fbx-maya ssc \r\n\r\nhttp://forum.mgear-framework.com/t/how-to-prevent-shear-on-joints/3252\r\n\r\nI had an absolute nightmare for several years with re-implementing ssc (segment scale compensation) in fbx-maya.\r\n\r\nCan you confirm?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4791584733/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4792027643","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4792027643","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":4792027643,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHaCJ-w","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-24T17:36:26Z","updated_at":"2026-06-24T18:06:33Z","body":"@fire This PR implements a different approach from Segment Scale Compensate. Rather, the PR by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/83903 is attempting to implement something like Segment Scale Compensate.\r\n\r\nAs explained in the description, I considered Segment Scale Compensate to have consistency issues with coordinate calculation systems in Godot's Node3D and other classes (such as Node2D/Skeleton/Physics/glTF IO/etc.), so https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120610 and this PR as one approach to address the need to \"dynamically change the thickness of bones (and skins)\".","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4792027643/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4794374635","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4794374635","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":4794374635,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHcRZ6w","user":{"login":"wagnerfs","id":106078,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjA3OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106078?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs","html_url":"https://github.com/wagnerfs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wagnerfs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-24T23:05:11Z","updated_at":"2026-06-24T23:05:11Z","body":"I'm a bit confused, does this mean we'd still need to update the rest bone positions to match the scale if we plan to stretch the bone? Or just updating the scale on the correct axis + pushing the child's position further on that axis would visually do it?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4794374635/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4796815808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4796815808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":4796815808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHemZwA","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-25T07:18:48Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T16:22:39Z","body":"For example, in a case where there is only one child on the Y-axis, you simply offset the child’s position along the Y-axis.In the method using Constraints, there is a demo that uses `ConvertTransform` to convert scaling into the child’s position. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120610\r\n\r\nHowever, in 1-vs-N cases like the \"Hand\", more calculations (although `bone_pose_position * scale` for each child) are required. If necessary, it might not be a bad idea to add a `SkeletonModifier` that reads `skin_scale` and automatically transforms the child’s position.\r\n\r\nThe reason the BoneExpander implementation stalled previously was that attempting to perform skin deformation within the SkeletonModifier caused instability. I believe it would be safe if the Skeleton handled skin scaling, while the BoneExpander only modified the bone positions.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4796815808/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4799361647","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4799361647","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":4799361647,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHhBybw","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-25T12:45:15Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T14:54:31Z","body":"I added \"BoneExpander3D\" now renamed \"BoneSpreader3D\". When using this modifier, positional shifts in the BoneEditor/IK Gizmo are tracked as a separate issue as https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117350, but there should be no problems with script control or runtime behavior.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1159\" height=\"610\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e5a5aef-97c2-40c1-9afd-f069b65419ab\" />\r\n\r\nBTW, since I reused the BoneExpander icon from when it was used for deforming Skin, it might be a little confusing as the icon for a \"Repositioning\" modifier. I’ll reconsider the icon later.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4799361647/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4802599448","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4802599448","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":4802599448,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHkHaGA","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-25T17:52:19Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T18:03:51Z","body":"What a coincidence. Just four days ago, I was trying to solve a problem in my project related to how to improve character customization by changing the player's height, head size, leg length, and everything else that can't be changed using Blend Shapes in Blender.\r\n\r\nIf I understand correctly, this PR can solve these problems?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4802599448/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4803794301","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4803794301","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":4803794301,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHlQVfQ","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-25T20:16:57Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T20:30:02Z","body":"@JekSun97 To be honest, it depends on your use case. For example, I think this feature would be useful in applications where the length of the arms and legs changes depending on the character's status.\r\n\r\nHowever, if you want to create a character model in Godot and export it or cases involving static scaling such as character creation, it generally makes more sense to set the bone pose scale to a pose like the T-pose and then bake (with a function similar to applying scale in Blender) it to bone rest, not the skin.\r\n\r\nWell, while this feature is primarily designed for dynamic scale changes, but it should work just fine if you’re not concerned with exporting or similar considerations.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4803794301/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887381778","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4887381778","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":4887381778,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0-HEg","user":{"login":"Fire551","id":52729867,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzI5ODY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52729867?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551","html_url":"https://github.com/Fire551","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fire551/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T19:49:45Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T20:08:05Z","body":"just tried it out and found it a far greater improvement in comparison to using non-deforming anchors to reset the scale, in readability and implementation. Though the BoneSpreader is a logical feature its slightly harder to intuitively use.\r\nI personally find this a extremely necessary improvement on skeletons, which i wish other game engines had. Though i wish there was a way to import animations that used this skin-scale- especially for squash and stretch in animations.\r\nIt'll be super helpful for VR body's, and as stated previously body customization. Its been fun seeing Godot go from a absolutely _terrible_ platform for XR to having request's like these that put other engines to shame.\r\n\r\nOn other matters when i tried it out i found that the build i used for the PR has no bone undo for skin-scale.\r\nand the `Reset all Bone Poses` button, logically, does not impact the skin-scale. \r\nThis makes it nigh impossible to notice which scales are modified, or a way to modify them en-mass.\r\n<img width=\"379\" height=\"812\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7bed3e4b-b44a-43ad-9bf7-04cf0c88857d\" />\r\n\r\nim also getting this weird scrolling effect, but im unsure if thats from this pull request or some mistake i made\r\n<img width=\"442\" height=\"369\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3ae6b5d9-859e-4836-b7e6-48309b9cc6d2\" />\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887381778/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4888022561","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4888022561","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":4888022561,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI1lOIQ","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T23:48:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T03:20:10Z","body":"I added the `revert` button on joint tree and the `reset_bone_skin_scale` option to `Skeleton3D.reset_bone_pose()`.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"351\" height=\"183\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/918c5761-44ec-486c-af3b-51e4de14e38d\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"605\" height=\"576\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/83223f9e-794c-4534-b363-47076c8096b3\" />\r\n\r\nGiven the use cases, I consider skin_scale to be relatively static, with attributes similar to rest, so I will make it possible to manage reset separately from pose. However, I have not implemented reset_skin_scale itself, as it is likely that there are almost no use cases where only this would be needed. Even if it were necessary, one could simply set it to Vector3(1, 1, 1).\r\n\r\n> Though i wish there was a way to import animations that used this skin-scale- especially for squash and stretch in animations.\r\n\r\nI believe this is difficult. As @fire indicated https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-4791584733 above, Segment Scale Compensate often has its own unique implementation in each application. Furthermore, while the blender importer imports via glTF, glTF itself does not have a field for Segment Scale Compensate.\r\n\r\n> im also getting this weird scrolling effect, but im unsure if thats from this pull request or some mistake i made\r\n\r\nThe broken scrolling appears to be a regression occurring in the 4.8 master branch, I've sent an issue #120991.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4888022561/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5381597052","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-5381597052","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":5381597052,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQMSnfA","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-22T17:09:06Z","updated_at":"2026-08-22T17:09:35Z","body":"gltf_document.cpp line 6016:\r\n```cpp\r\n@@ -6012,6 +6013,8 @@ void GLTFDocument::_convert_mesh_instances(Ref<GLTFState> p_state) {\r\n                                        if (bind_name == StringName()) {\r\n                                                bind_name = godot_skeleton->get_bone_name(bone_i);\r\n                                        }\r\n+                                       Vector3 skin_scale = godot_skeleton->get_bone_skin_scale(bone_i);\r\n+                                       bind_pose = bind_pose.scaled(skin_scale);\r\n                                        GLTFNodeIndex skeleton_bone_i = gltf_skeleton->joints[bone_i];\r\n                                        gltf_skin->joints_original.push_back(skeleton_bone_i);\r\n                                        gltf_skin->joints.push_back(skeleton_bone_i);\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5381597052/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5382435082","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-5382435082","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":5382435082,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQNFxCg","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-22T20:27:10Z","updated_at":"2026-08-22T20:27:10Z","body":"I and @fire both want the change always added to the gltf export code because it matches the behavior of bone pose.\r\n\r\nI understand there's an issue that skeleton modifiers do not currently get exported, and if people want the modifiers exported, that should be a separate pull request.\r\n\r\nIf a user does not want to export skin_scale, they can use the reset bone poses & skin scale option in the Skeleton3D menu before exporting.\r\n\r\nBut there are uses for skin_scale without using modifiers, so that's why I would like to always export skin scale, even if modifiers are not exported.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5382435082/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5382462303","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120609#issuecomment-5382462303","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120609","id":5382462303,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQNHbXw","user":{"log